-- title:
--   Completed stalk at a supersingular point as Drinfeld chart
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$.
--
--   Field and level data. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subset L((q)) =$ `LaurentSeries L` with
--   $$K = \mathtt{laurentBaseChange}\,L\bigl(\mathtt{xHFunctionField}\,((q\ell)^2M')\,(\mathtt{levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M')\bigr),$$
--   that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of $\mathbb{Q} \subset \mathbb{Q}((q))$ attached to the level $(q\ell)^2M'$ and to the subgroup $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$).
--
--   Base ring. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $\varpi \in A$ be a uniformiser, $\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series `coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`, where [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1}\cdot jNumQ$ is the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant. Finally let $t \in A$ satisfy $t^{q-1} = q\,w$ for some unit $w$ of $A$ (hypothesis `ht`).
--
--   The point. Let $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the scheme obtained as the pushout of the two morphisms `fFin` and `fInf`, i.e. glued from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin A K j` $=$ `chartAlg A K {j}` and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebra at infinity, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}$ and let $\varpi z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathcal{O}_\mathfrak{X}$ obtained from $\varpi$ through `toBase` (hypothesis `hϖz`); it is assumed (`hz`) that $\varpi z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$, so that $z$ is a point of the special fibre. Let $y$ be a point of `XFin` $= \operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j)$ with `ιFin`$(y) = z$. Supersingularity (`hss`): for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   Conclusion. Then there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$ (a domain, a discrete valuation ring, and adically complete for $\mathfrak{m}_W$), a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W\langle\!\langle X_0, X_1\rangle\!\rangle =$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W` with $u$ and $v$ units and
--   $$f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0, X_1)^{q+2},$$
--   the subtracted term being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18), and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W\langle\!\langle X_0, X_1\rangle\!\rangle/\bigl(C(\sigma t)\,v - f\,u\bigr),$$
--   where the completion is the adic completion of the stalk $STK = \mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ at its maximal ideal, with the following seven properties. Here $CMP$ denotes that completion, $toC : STK \to CMP$ the canonical map, $mkS$ the quotient map onto $S$, and $germY$ the canonical map from the finite chart algebra to $STK$ obtained from the open immersion `ιFin` (global sections of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebra, transported to sections over the image open set, followed by the germ at $z$).
--
--   (1) Compatibility with the base: for every $a \in A$, $e$ sends the image in $CMP$ of the germ at $z$ of the section attached to $a$ through `toBase` to $mkS(C(\sigma a))$.
--
--   (2) Stability of the finite chart: for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') H γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), the subalgebra `chartAlgFin A K j` is mapped into itself by $\tau$. (The predicate `IsLevelAutAt` asserts that for every weight $k$, every pair $f, g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, the series attached to $p_g$ being nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image under `coeffEmb` of the quotient of the series attached to $p_f$ and $p_g$, and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, one has $\iota_*(\tau x)\cdot(\text{$q$-expansion of } g|_k \mathtt{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}) = (\text{$q$-expansion of } f|_k \mathtt{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1})$; so $\tau$ realises the deck transformation attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, conjugated at level $q\ell$.)
--
--   (3) Triviality modulo $y$ at level $\ell$: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$, every $\tau$ as in (2) for this $\gamma$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves the finite chart algebra, the restriction of $\tau$ to that algebra satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for all $a$ in it.
--
--   (4) Semilinear action on the chart: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau$ as in (2), every proof that $\tau$ preserves the finite chart algebra, and under the assumption that the restricted $\tau$ satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for all $a$ in that algebra, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{M}_2(W)$ such that: (a) $\theta(e(toC(germY\,a))) = e(toC(germY(\tau a)))$ for all $a$ in the finite chart algebra; (b) $\theta(mkS(C(w))) = mkS(C(w))$ for all $w \in W$; (c) for each index $jj$, $\theta(mkS(X_{jj})) - mkS\bigl(\sum_{ii} C(M_{ii\,jj})X_{ii}\bigr)$ lies in the square of the ideal of $S$ generated by $mkS(X_0), mkS(X_1)$; (d) $c^{q+1} - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; (e) $M_{ii\,jj} - c\,\gamma_{ii\,jj} \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ for all $ii, jj$; (f) if $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ then $c - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; (g) if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$, then $c - 1 \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   (5) Separation of branches: for all integers $a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ such that each $P_i$ fails to contain at least one of $mkS(X_0), mkS(X_1)$, both contain $mkS(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and for each $i$ there is $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ with $mkS(C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h) \in P_i$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ in $\mathbb{Z}$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $toC$ followed by $e$ (a ring homomorphism $STK \to S$) are distinct ideals of the stalk.
--
--   (6) Valuative description of one branch: for every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ failing to contain at least one of $mkS(X_0), mkS(X_1)$, containing $mkS(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and such that $mkS(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h) \in P$ for some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra: $toC(germY\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$, viewed in $L((q))$, lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ under $A \to L$.
--
--   (7) Hasse chart clause: there exist a proof that the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the image of `jqModC L` under `qExpand L (q*ℓ)`) belongs to $K$, a proof that the resulting element of $K$ belongs to the finite chart algebra, an element $a_0 \in A$ together with a proof that the difference of that element of the chart algebra and the image of $a_0$ lies in $y$, a natural number $e_0 \ge 1$, and a power series $h \in (X_0, X_1)^{e_0}$, such that: for all $a, b \in W$ with at least one of $a, b$ outside $\mathfrak{m}_W$ and with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, the element $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^i b^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$; and $e\bigl(toC(germY(\,\mathtt{jqNModC}\text{-element} - a_0))\bigr) = mkS(h)$.
--
--   This is the local structure theorem at a supersingular point of the special fibre for the two-chart integral model over $A$ of the $j$-line inside the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$: the completed stalk is identified with a Drinfeld-type local chart $W\langle\!\langle X_0,X_1\rangle\!\rangle/(C(\sigma t)v - fu)$ whose leading form is $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$, together with the linearisation of the deck transformations (clauses (2)–(4)), the separation of the branches through the point (clauses (5)–(6)) and the unit-leading-form (Hasse) description of the normalised $j$-invariant on the chart (clause (7)). It is the form of the statement for a general base $A$ with algebraically closed residue field and a general constant $t$ with $t^{q-1} = q\cdot(\text{unit})$, and it is used for the construction of supersingular affine charts and for the computation of the inertia action on the Drinfeld chart through its linear part and the tame character.
